/-!
# Concrete higher-rank and unitary Borel torus injections

Field units inject into the actual PSL₃ flag Borel, the Sp₄ flag Borel
restricted to Sp₄′, and the PSU₃ root–torus Borel. In the unitary case the
field is the Hermitian fixed subfield, whose order is proved to be 2^f;
actual basis and conjugation equivalences also give every Sylow normalizer.
These model calculations discharge the torus inputs to the quotient-lifting
argument in `BorelReduction.Quotients`. Recognition of the source component
and the final oddness deduction remain with the parent case assembly.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, E.2.2, printed pp.215–216, and 15.3.65, printed
p.1152 (`refs/quasithin.pdf`, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004).
-/
